  "body": "### Summary\nAs a respondent, I want to see the current app next to the proposals, so that I compare on real screens.\n\n### Scope\n- Screenshots of the current app (4.0.4, `master`): reading a topic on iPhone; sidebar and current layout on iPad; inner and cover screens of the iPhone Duo.\n- One public topic for every screenshot, pseudos masked.\n- 10-second videos for the Duo.\n- No proposal classed Non visible (for example no page scrubber).\n\n### Deliverable\n`docs/ux/questionnaire/visuels/actuel/`.\n\n### Model and review\nSonnet on the Mac, Opus review. Brief: `docs/ux/cadrage-agents-questionnaire.md` §3, UX-07.\n\nTracked on #628.\n\n### Before you start\n\nRead, in order: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`, `docs/agents/LESSONS.md`, then `docs/ux/README.md`. The UX documents are in French. Until the docs PR is merged into `dev-swift`, read them on branch `docs/ux-questionnaire`.\n\nRules: no proposal the PO classed **Non** may appear in the survey (`docs/ux/tri-m5-decisions.md` §3.5 and §4.7). The reader keeps the WebView: the survey only shows improvements possible with it. Stop and report if an instruction contradicts the plan.\n\n---\n_Opened with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) for the PO (Bruno), 2026-11-07._\n\n",
